# Git metadata — including the .git dirs inside the checked-out siblings under
# .deps/, which are large and never needed by the build.
.git
**/.git
.gitignore
.githooks/

# CI / tooling config not read by the build
.github/
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.obsidian/
.opencode/
graphify-out/

# Documentation
*.md
docs/

# Development files
.env.example
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.local
**/Dockerfile.local
.air.toml

# Build artifacts
bin/
tmp/
*.log
*.exe

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Dependencies vendored on the host (downloaded inside the image instead)
vendor/

# NOTE ON WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED
#   .deps/          — the checked-out maintainerd-kit / maintainerd-sdk siblings.
#                     go.mod replaces point at them and the build repoints those
#                     replaces at ./.deps/*, so ignoring this dir breaks the build.
#                     See the Dockerfile header.
#   gen/            — generated protobuf/gRPC code the build compiles against.
#   migrations/     — embedded into the binary via migrations/embed.go.
#   web/console/    — source for the SPA build stage.

# Test files and coverage — not compiled into the production binary
*_test.go
tests/
coverage.*
*.out
web/**/coverage/

# Frontend deps / build output / secrets — rebuilt inside the image, never
# copied from the host (would bloat context and leak local env).
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.env
.env
*.env
